@@s001 Missing data, outliers and the multivariate normal
@@s002 dato:the 10 people,due:mean,ora:two new people,no:outlier,ok:normal
@@s003 Again height and weight: the cloud is narrow and elongated, because the two variables are strongly correlated (0.995).
@@s004 Two new people arrive. <b>A</b> = (190 cm, 55 kg), <b>B</b> = (190 cm, 78 kg).
@@s005 Euclidean distance from the mean: A <b>20.7</b>, B <b>21.2</b>. Almost equal. Also the z-scores taken one at a time are moderate (A: +1.16 and −1.04; B: +1.16 and +1.13): none exceeds 3.
@@s006 <b>Mahalanobis</b> distance, which uses the covariance: A <b>21.4</b>, B <b>1.17</b>. B follows the correlation (tall and heavy), A goes against it (tall but light): A is a <b>multivariate outlier</b>.
